WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.070
- You have written so many amazing songs.

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.900
Do you remember your first
song like you ever wrote?

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.207
- First song I wrote was in sixth grade.

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:10.020
"Here I Go Falling in Love Again."

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.000
- You were this guy in the sixth grade?

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.350
I love it.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.550
- I was that guy in sixth grade.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.680
Saw a girl and fell in love with her,

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:21.210
and I used my brother's
friend's guitar of a cousin

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.920
and it was a right-handed guitar.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:23.753
I picked it up

00:00:23.753 --> 00:00:26.700
and learned some chords and
wrote this song for her.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:27.810
She never heard it.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:28.643
- She never heard it?

00:00:28.643 --> 00:00:29.610
You never played it for her?

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.080
- No, it was the first
song I wrote for her

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.090
and it was also, I
wrote two songs for her.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.620
'Cause that was in sixth grade

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.330
and eighth grade she broke my heart

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.610
and I wrote, yeah, she did.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:39.600
- Yeah, she did.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:40.710
Well, where she now?

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.680
- So, I wrote my second song

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.270
called "The Bitter Taste of Life."

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.620
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.453
- Eighth grade.

00:00:47.453 --> 00:00:48.840
- Do you feel like,

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.340
I feel like circumstances like that,

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.230
I have something similar
whenever I was younger

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.250
that happened to me.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.350
I still can go back to that place

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.472
and use that fuel to write.

00:00:57.472 --> 00:00:58.305
- That's it.

00:00:58.305 --> 00:00:59.160
That's what I use so many times

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.166
for writing songs is
all those crazy times.

00:01:02.166 --> 00:01:03.240
- Because that depth when you're so young.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:04.201
- Yep.

00:01:04.201 --> 00:01:05.034
- And it's so...
- So passionate.

00:01:05.034 --> 00:01:06.360
- Fresh and passionate.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.040
'Cause people always think,
"Oh, they're too young to feel."

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.140
I'm like, you feel
everything when you're young.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.430
- You feel it in such a big way.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:12.360
- Yeah.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:13.560
- And you're not jaded at that point.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:14.393
- It's pure.

00:01:14.393 --> 00:01:15.226
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:15.226 --> 00:01:16.950
We end up doing another song
called "Water Runs Dry."

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:17.783
- That's what I mean.

00:01:17.783 --> 00:01:18.616
That's what I mean, "Water Runs Dry."

00:01:18.616 --> 00:01:19.449
I thought that's where you were going.

00:01:19.449 --> 00:01:20.282
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:20.282 --> 00:01:21.240
Because I love how it starts out.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.860
- So that went back, you know,

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.270
to that sixth grade kid again.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:25.350
- Yeah.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.540
Once again, maybe you should
write a thank you letter

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:28.373
to this lady.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.290
Maybe we all should right now.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:34.347
Just get out our Pilot
G2 Pen and go to town.

00:01:34.347 --> 00:01:35.999
I'm just saying.

00:01:35.999 --> 00:01:38.400
That woman helped us out tremendously

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.160
with our own relationships via your music.

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.020
- It's funny because years later

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.459
I ended up tracking her down.

00:01:46.459 --> 00:01:47.400
- Did you?

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.233
- Yeah.

00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:50.010
'Cause I wanted to talk to her

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.133
and see if I remembered
everything the same.

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:53.340
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.313
- And it was pretty close.

00:01:55.313 --> 00:01:56.197
- What did she say?

00:01:56.197 --> 00:01:58.477
"Yeah, no, I wasn't into it."

00:01:58.477 --> 00:02:00.360
"Yeah, no, just a real quick recap.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:01.830
I didn't want you."

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.450
What did that conversation go like?

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:06.697
- She said that she didn't,
she ultimately said,

00:02:06.697 --> 00:02:08.510
"I spent most of my life

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:10.350
always thinking about people that hurt me.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:11.790
I never thought about the people

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.530
that I may have hurt along the way."

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:14.363
She was sorry for it.

00:02:14.363 --> 00:02:15.930
- Write that song, sir.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.010
- Exactly.

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:18.000
- That's a great lyric.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:18.991
- It was a great lyric.

00:02:18.991 --> 00:02:22.928
And I said, I said to
her, "Don't apologize.

00:02:22.928 --> 00:02:24.900
It's because of you,

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.900
you launched the kid that
wrote a thousand songs."

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.100
- Yeah.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.488
With 80 Grammy nominations.

00:02:31.488 --> 00:02:32.580
It's crazy, yeah.

